# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. morgan's first conversation.

~ start
set morgan_met
Narrator: Bundles of dried yarrow and bog-mint brush your shoulders, and glass vials clink softly on crooked shelves. Morgan looks up with faraway green eyes, fingers stained violet with crushed roots.
morgan [smile]: Oh, come in, mind the low beam by the door. I was just labelling the willow-water, or perhaps I already finished that an hour ago.
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask about their remedies and work -> about_self
* Ask how long they have lived in Wickermoor -> about_village
* Ask about the stranger vials on the back shelf -> rumour
* [Medicine DC 13] Notice the gaps in their ledger notes -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
morgan [neutral]: Was there another draught you needed, or did we only just begin talking?
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask about their remedies and work -> about_self
* Ask how long they have lived in Wickermoor -> about_village
* Ask about the stranger vials on the back shelf -> rumour
* [Medicine DC 13] Notice the gaps in their ledger notes -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
morgan [smile]: The red bottles mend torn flesh properly, and the herb bundles mostly comfort the locals, though comfort does half the curing.
shop
-> menu

~ about_self
morgan [neutral]: I have no beds for the sick, only bottles and poultices to carry home. People tell me their aches, and I try to remember which jar eased them last time.
-> menu

~ about_village
morgan [weary]: Everyone in the hollow has an old name and an older grave to tend. Sometimes I wonder what sort of name I had before the moor took me in.
-> menu

~ rumour
morgan [sly]: Some nights I brew tinctures that let a drinker see through mist or hear what the dead whisper in the thatch. I never quite recall who taught me the measure.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: The open ledger on Morgan's counter has whole pages torn short, with ink trails stopping mid-word as if the hand simply froze.
morgan [sad]: Funny thing, the clock strikes one bell and when I blink it is striking the next. I woke here small and alone, and the years between still slip through my fingers.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
Narrator: Morgan gently closes the stained ledger under a bundle of dried chamomile.
morgan [smile]: Do not mind my messy handwriting, nobody in the hollow can read apothecary scrawl anyway.
-> menu
